<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson results by business area.</title>
<headline>Ericsson results by business area.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group LM Ericsson AB on Tuesday posted a 31 percent rise in order bookings to 138.05 billion crowns.</p>
<p>This included a 31 percent rise in order intake in its radio communications or mobile telephone unit and a 56 percent rise in the public telecommunications unit.  </p>
<p> BUSINESS UNIT-ORDER BOOKINGS (MLN SKR) 96  vs   '95</p>
<p> Radio communication		    84,213  vs  64,046</p>
<p> Public telecommunication	     33,038  vs  21,187</p>
<p> Business networks			16,324  vs  16,359</p>
<p> Components				  8,102  vs   8,157</p>
<p> Microwave systems			 4,512  vs   3,061</p>
<p> Other operations			  2,789  vs   2,183</p>
<p> Less intersegment sales     CHARGE 10,930  vs  10,012 CHARGE</p>
<p> TOTALS				    138,048  vs 104,981</p>
<p> BUSINESS UNIT-TURNOVER (MLN SKR)   '96	  '95</p>
<p> Radio communication		    79,101  vs  56,358</p>
<p> Public telecommunication	     25,185  vs  23,575</p>
<p> Business networks			15,932  vs  14,094</p>
<p> Components				  7,793  vs   7,721</p>
<p> Microwave systems			 4,330  vs   3,682</p>
<p> Other operations			  2,789  vs   2,183</p>
<p> Less intersegment sales     CHARGE 10,864  vs   8,833 CHARGE</p>
<p> TOTALS				    124,266  vs  98,780</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
